# $vault_name — conventions

What *this* vault has decided. `CLAUDE.md` is the schema every crate vault shares; this file is the part that's only true here.

Read it alongside `CLAUDE.md`, at the start of every session.

**This file is mine, and the engine never writes it.** `crate init` created it once and `crate upgrade` leaves it alone from then on, so anything here survives every release. That is the whole reason it exists: `CLAUDE.md` is overwritten on upgrade, so a rule written there is a rule that gets lost.

It refines the schema; it never overrides it. A convention names something `CLAUDE.md` deliberately leaves open — how a particular kind of page is titled, say. If a rule here appears to contradict one there, that's a bug in one of them: show me both rather than picking a side.

## Conventions

Nothing yet.

An empty list is a normal state, not a gap for you to fill. A convention gets written when a real decision gets made and I want it to hold next time — don't invent one to put here, and don't infer one from what the vault happens to look like today. If you notice the wiki following an unwritten rule that would be worth keeping, say so and I'll write it down.
